{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:OrganicChemistry.ChainRingComparison","@type":"LeanModule","name":"OrganicChemistry.ChainRingComparison","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Even","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Common"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Organic.barrier_grows_with_ring_size","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Organic.barrier_grows_with_ring_size","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/organic-chemistry/chain-ring-comparison.lean#L47-L53","doc":"The barrier prediction for even-N rings:\nΔE ∝ (N-1) - N/2 = (N-2)/2.\nFor N=6: ΔE ∝ 2. For N=8: ΔE ∝ 3. Etc. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Organic.alexanderWeightDifference","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Organic.alexanderWeightDifference","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/organic-chemistry/chain-ring-comparison.lean#L39-L45","doc":"The linking-number difference between chain and threaded ring.\nFor even N: (N-1) - N/2 = (N-2)/2.  Mirrors the definition in\n`QOU.Organic.alexanderWeightDifference` (ring-closure-barrier);\nrepeated here so this content-block sibling compiles standalone. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:ring-closure-barrier","label":"conj:ring-closure-barrier","md":"quantum-observable-universe/organic-chemistry/ring-closure-barrier.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Organic.benzene_weights","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Organic.benzene_weights","kind":"theorem","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/organic-chemistry/chain-ring-comparison.lean#L32-L37","doc":"For benzene (N=6): chain linking number is 5, ring linking number is 3,\ndifference is 2. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:chain-ring-comparison","label":"conj:chain-ring-comparison","md":"quantum-observable-universe/organic-chemistry/chain-ring-comparison.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Organic.threading_efficiency_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Organic.threading_efficiency_half","kind":"theorem","line":23,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/organic-chemistry/chain-ring-comparison.lean#L23-L30","doc":"The threading efficiency ratio for even-N rings is always 1/2:\nlk(T(2,N)) / N = (N/2) / N = 1/2, with lk the linking number. ","signatureChunk":0}]}